* '''Ambulacraria''' ancestor
** bilaterally symmetrical
** stalked attached?
** soft body
** tentacles to either side of mouth, likely branched
** pharyngeal basket-feeder?
** straight-(ish)? gut?
* ''Yanjiahella'':
** bilaterally symmetrical
** stalked attached
** plated (stereom?) theca
** free-moving (coelemic? water vascular?) tentacle on each side of a central mouth
** pharyngeal basket-feeder?
** straight gut
* ''Ctenoimbricata'':
** bilaterally symmetrical
** ground-dwelling
** stereom-plated theca
** recumbant (coelemic? water vascular? tentacles on each side of a central mouth
** ctenidium around mouth and lateral tentacle grooves
** pharyngeal basket-feeder
** straight gut
** '''Ctenocystoidea''':
*** near-bilaterally symmetrical
*** ground-dwelling
*** stereom-plated theca
*** ambulacra on either side of a central mouth
*** ctenidum around ambulacra, articulated
*** pharyngeal basket-feeder
*** straight gut
** '''Cincta''':
*** asymmetrical, torsion during ontogeny
*** ground-dwelling, rigid stele-anchored
*** stereom-plated theca
*** ambulacra always on left, sometimes also present but shorter on right
*** labrum and operculum 
*** u-shaped gut
*** '''Soluta''':
**** asymmetrical, variable torsion during ontogeny
**** stalked, initially attahed then ground-dwelling w/muscular stele
**** stereom-plated theca
**** single free-moving ambulacrum covering the mouth, left coleom
**** ambulacral feeder, brachiole-style (but not actual brachiole)
**** straight-ish gut
*** '''Stylophora''':
**** asymmetrical, torsion during ontogeny
**** ground-dwelling, rigid posterior appendages for positioning
**** stereom-plated theca
**** single free-moving ambulacrum leading to mouth, left coleom
**** ambulacral feeder, arm-style (but perhaps not actual crinoid arm)
**** u-shaped gut
*** '''Helicoplacoidea'''
**** spiral tri-radial symmetry, of a sort, torsion lateral mouth, apical anus
**** ground-dwelling, likely attached
**** stereom-plated theca
**** left ambulacrum has triplicated (A, B-C, D-E), anus between B-C and D-E
**** ambulacral feeder, mouth at center of three ambulacra
**** u-shaped gut
**** ''Helicocystis''
***** spiral 1-2-2 pentaradial symmetry, torsion apical mouth, far lateral anus
***** stalked (short) attached
***** stereom-plated theca
***** B-C and D-E ambulacra now split, anus between C and D
***** ambulacral feeder, mouth at center of A, B-C, D-E
***** u-shaped gut
**** '''Eocrinoidea'''
***** 1-2-2 crypto-helical pentaradial symmetry, torsion apical mouth, anus
***** stalked attached
***** stereom-plated theca
***** B-C and D-E ambulacra split, anus between C and D
***** ambulacral feeder, mouth at center of A, B-C, D-E
***** u-shaped gut
**** '''Edrioasteroidea'''
***** 1-2-2 pentaradial symmetry, torsion apical mouth, anus on same surface
***** flat-to-short-stalked attached
***** stereom-plated theca
***** B-C and D-E ambulacra split, anus between C and D
***** ambulacral feeder, mouth at center of A, B-C, D-E
***** u-shaped gut
***** ''Camptostroma''
***** 1-2-2 pentaradial symmetry, torsion apical mouth, anus on same surface
***** flat attached, cupcake walls
***** stereom-plated theca
***** B-C and D-E ambulacra split, anus between C and D
***** ambulacral feeder, mouth at center of A, B-C, D-E
***** u-shaped gut


